Chris and I got to talking last night about rogues.  Since we now have so many rogues, I thought I would try and dredge up my old theoritical max BackStab dmg based on weapon and level spreedsheet.  <P>Couldn't find it.<P>So...I built a new one, it collapsed and sank into the swamp.<P>So I built a new one...<P>No..wait..wrong idiom.    <IMG SRC="biggrin.gif" border="0"><P>Anyway...<P>Summary:<P>Based on the information gleaned from The Safehouse archives on how BS is calculated and how MAX Dmg is calculated.<P>STR playes a HUGE role in a rogue's BS calculations.  At 31'st...each 10pts of STR adds about 3% to total max BS.<P>Starting at 25th...every 3 levels a rogue will see a nice jump in BS dmg output.  I believe the same can be said for all melee classes max dmg, but since max dmg plays a key role in max BS calcs...rogues will notice the effect more.<P>I will post the link to the .xls here as soon as I get home and can upload it to the website for you all to play with and critic.<p>[ July 13, 2001: Message edited by: Verser ]<P>--------------------<P>Verser - Bard of the 51st Song
