Just a little something for all our rogues to look forward to...<P>Sendil with a 173 STR, and a 13 damage piercer, backstabbed for a max of 321 at 49th level.  I have yet to get a higher BS than that with him.  He consistently BS's for around 190-220.  The problem with that kind of damage is aggro.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0">  If you rogues haven't been practicing on evade and aggro management, i would HIGHLY suggest you do.  It doesn't take long for mobs to make a greasy stain out of you at higher levels if you can't manage the aggro you build up.  <P>While STR does play a large part in big backstab numbers, weapon damage is almost as big a factor.  Again with Sendil.  At 173 STR, 8 damage piercer, 49th level, max BS was 211.  At 173 STR, 10 damage piercer, 49th level, max BS was 261.  Thats a difference of 110 points between the 8 dmg and 13 dmg.  Not only is your max affected, but average is affected also.  I seem to average about 2/3rds of my max when I backstab.  with a max of 211 that would be an average of about 140.  pretty measly numbers.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0">  So, in other words... lets get our rogues some better weapons and STR gear. hehe<P>--------------------<P>Lownar Baardeth - 55th Level Gnecromancer<BR>Kalaan - 30th Level Rogue<BR>Rakasak Smakatak - 21st Level Monk<BR>Bertox. Server
