Perfect!  Thanks for posting your ACTUAL numbers Sendil, that gives us a starting point so we can actually prove/disprove any damage formulas quickly.  This is a cut/paste from the safehouse FAQ on rogues:<P><B><BR>2.7.1 How is backstab damage calculated? <BR>Nothing is official, but the general belief is that at low levels, it works something like this: Assuming that you are using a weapon deemed 'acceptable' for your level (i.e. not too powerful [some players report getting very high level weapons at lower levels and not getting the damage they were supposed to until they leveled some more]), max damage is calculated as: <P>(DMG * 2) + 1 + ((level - 25)/3) + ((STR+SKILL)/100) <P>Backstab simply multiplies this by a constant factor. We approximate this factor to be: <P>(BACKSTAB_SKILL / 25) <BR></B><P><BR>Ok, here is my math with my results (following in parenthisis by Sendil's actual seen value)  Note that prior to level 51, backstab maxes at 200.  I have used skill=200, STR=173 and my examples use Sendil's 13 damage, 8 damage and then finally 10 damage weapons for comparison:<P>(13*2)+1+((49-25)/3) + ((173+200)/100)  *  (200/25)<BR>26+1+(24/3)+(373/100)  *  8  =  309.8 (Sendil 321)<P>(8*2)+1+((49-25)/3) + ((173+200)/100)  *  (200/25)<BR>16+1+(24/3)+(373/100)  *  8  =  229.8 (Sendil 211)<P>(10*2)+1+((49-25)/3) + ((173+200)/100)  *  (200/25)<BR>20+1+(24/3)+(373/100)  *  8  =  261.8 (261)<P>These formulas calculate max damage very closely with what Sendil is actually seeing in the game.  Since the damage 10 seems to be right on, I'll use that as my example, and I will take 100 strength away from Sendil (sorry man):<P>(10*2)+1+((49-25/3) + ((73+200)/100)  *  (200/25)<BR>20+1+(24/3)+(273/100)  *  8  =  253<P>Max damage went from 261 all the way to 253.  Big whoop.  Like I've said many times before, STR really doesn't add up to jack in the game, especially considering 100 STR is a heck of a lot to be throwing around, had I done this example with a 5 or 10 difference in strength the change in max damage would be almost negligable.<P>Please feel free to comment, or correct any math errors I may have made.<p>[ July 13, 2001: Message edited by: Heelir, Brod and Shato ]
</FONT>
