I also went to the Safehouse; however...in thier forum library section.  If you look further down on the "Rogue FAQ" thread there is a topic buried down a little deeper that gives an updated Max Dmg formula.<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">quote:</font><HR><BR>3.1.1 How much damage can I do in combat? <BR>At low levels, the maximum you will see is (2 * DMG) + 1. At 18 and beyond, you will notice the +1 become +2, +3, +4 etc. Beldukil at the Paladins of Norrath site has done extensive work on how damage is determined. He has developed some empirical formula for maximum and minimum damage which are:<P>MAX DAMAGE = (((STR+SKILL)/100)*DAM)+ LEVELBONUS<P>where LEVELBONUS = ((LEVEL-25)/3)+1<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This formula differs from the one listed in the original max dmg formula in that it has the "*DAM" added.  That places a much highier emphasis on the STR portion of the equation.<P>The easiest way to to confirm this for max damage ( not max BS ) is to try hitting stuff with low STR, then buffed STR.  Paying attention to what your MAX DMG from just hitting seems to be.<P>Using that formula for a 49th rogue w/ 13dmg:<BR>173 STR = 59 DMG<BR>073 STR = 46 DMG<P>When you plug those numbers into the regular BS calc...you end up with a MUCH highier BUFFED BS Damage over the un-buffed.<P>Also..based on the caclulated numbers and observed data from Sendil...I'd have to disaggree with what the caclulation is trying to say...it just seems WAAAY highier then what Sendil has achieved.  This is assuming Sendil's BS skill is maxed too.<P>I will say that there is a noticable difference in BS damage with Meeka when buffed and unbuffed...even a 25 Point STR buff seemed to make a good difference in her BS's.<P>--------------------<P>Verser - Bard of the 51st Song
