Ok, this was bugging me, so I came up with this little program, it gets me fairly close to my observed numbers.  I will have to do some more testing with Sendil and get more accurate numbers, as I can't recall for absolute sure that the numbers I gave were 100% correct.  With that said, these calcs seem to get pretty close to what I remembered.  I am pretty sure that your attack rating has something to do with how your damage is calculated.  I have observed that 5 points of strength = 4 points of attack.  That may vary according to class though.  Anyway, here is the program.<P>def var v-lev as int label "Level" init 50.<BR>def var v-dam as int label "Damage" init 13.<BR>def var v-str as int label "STR" init 173.<BR>def var v-basestr as int label "Base STR" init 125.<BR>def var v-skill as int label "Skill" init 210.<BR>def var v-mod as dec label "Modifier".<BR>def var v-bsmod as dec label "BS Mod".<BR>def var v-maxbs as dec label "Max BS".<BR>def var v-maxdam as dec.<BR>def var v-attk as int label "ATTK" init 930.<BR>def var v-strdiff as int.<BR>def var v-calc1 as dec.<BR>def var v-calc2 as dec.<BR>def var v-calc3 as dec.<BR>def var v-calc4 as dec.<P>update   <BR>v-dam   <BR>v-basestr   <BR>v-str   <BR>v-skill<BR>with frame abc.<P>assign   <BR>v-mod = (v-lev / 7)   <BR>v-bsmod = ((v-attk) / 100)   <BR>v-strdiff = (v-str - v-basestr)   <BR>v-calc1 = ((v-str + v-skill) / 100)   <BR>v-calc2 = ((v-attk) / 100)   <BR>v-calc3 = ((v-dam * 2) + 1)   <BR>v-maxdam = ((v-calc1 * v-calc2) + (v-dam * 1.5))   <BR>v-maxbs = (v-calc2 * (v-calc3 + v-mod)).<P>display   <BR>v-mod   <BR>v-calc1   <BR>v-calc2   <BR>v-calc3   <BR>v-maxdam   <BR>v-maxbs<BR>with frame xyz.<P>--------------------<P>Lownar Baardeth - 55th Level Gnecromancer<BR>Kalaan - 30th Level Rogue<BR>Rakasak Smakatak - 21st Level Monk<BR>Bertox. Server
